Subject: Decode simple-signing policy keys with github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp/armor
Origin: DHI-internal (dependency remediation)
Advisory: GO-2026-5932
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/IBM/portieris 66c76b98ce0d7cd929bd073ff7cf69d51902fc04
Verify: cmd `go list -tags containers_image_openpgp -f '{{.Imports}}' ./pkg/verifier/simple` expect "github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp/armor"
Forwarded: no (not yet proposed to IBM/portieris)
Drop-When: upstream >= 0.16.3 (once pkg/verifier/simple/gpgArmour.go no longer imports golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp)

decodeArmoredKey is the only importer of golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp in the
portieris binary. That package tree is frozen and deprecated upstream, and its
advisory lists every package in it, armor included. The ProtonMail fork is the
maintained replacement the advisory names, exposes the same armor.Decode and
Block API, returns io.EOF when no armor block is found, and is already linked
because go.podman.io/image/v5 verifies signatures with it under the
containers_image_openpgp build tag. After this change the binary links no
golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package; upstream's gpgArmour_test.go table tests
run unchanged in the package build.

diff --git a/pkg/verifier/simple/gpgArmour.go b/pkg/verifier/simple/gpgArmour.go
--- a/pkg/verifier/simple/gpgArmour.go
+++ b/pkg/verifier/simple/gpgArmour.go
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ import (
 	"fmt"
 	"io/ioutil"

-	"golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp/armor"
+	"github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp/armor"
 )

